<title>GERMANY: SPD's Schroeder - meeting EMU goals needed for trust.</title>
<headline>SPD's Schroeder - meeting EMU goals needed for trust.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gerhard Schroeder, a leading figure in Germany's opposition Social Democrats, said on Thursday that the criteria for membership of European monetary union must be met to ensure the trust of the financial markets.</p>
<p>&quot;If the criteria are not held to, then people will not believe in the euro, and the financial markets will not believe in the euro,&quot; Schroeder said, adding that this could lead to interest rate hikes.</p>
<p>Schroeder was speaking in a debate on monetary union on German television.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
